00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.000
In the sense, something which is baffles the imagination.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:33.000
God chooses to dwell among us, with the Jewish people.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:39.000
The word Mishkan, from which two other words derive, I'll tell you in a minute.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.000
One means Shachan, to dwell.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
And the other word Shekhinah.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Shekhinah means the dwelling of God.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Now, God chooses to dwell in the Mishkan.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
What does it mean?

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
It means like this.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Suppose I ask you,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.000
I mean, within the scheme of the Tora,

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.000
What is the highest point of the universe?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.000
So you would say, the highest point of the universe is the Shamaim,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.000
where the Malachim are,

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.000
the throne of God.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.000
That's what you say.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Of course, when you say that, you know, Malachim, angels, heavens.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
Here, the Tora has a revolutionary idea.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.000
It says no.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.000
The highest point of the universe,

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.000
is where God dwells.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.000
And the dwelling place of God,

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.000
is not in heavens,

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.000
is on earth.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.000
This is a revolutionary idea.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Means, in a sense,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.000
that the Malachim have to pray to God,

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.000
who is in the Aris.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.000
You know, I mean, this, you have to inverse,

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.000
through the whole notion of the Mishkan,

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.000
the relationship,

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.000
the whole structure of the universe is inversed.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.000
In other words, if God is Shekhin,

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.000
as we are going to say here, in the Mishkan,

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:12.000
means therefore, that the angels, they have to look up to whom?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.000
To God. Where is God?

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.000
On earth.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.000
No.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.000
This, no.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.000
This is the notion of the Mishkan.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.000
The Mishkan means, that from now on,

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.000
God, in a sense, switches addresses.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.000
The address of God is changed.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.000
He changes addresses.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.000
In what way He changes addresses?

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.000
He is no longer Shekhin,

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.000
but Meromim.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.000
But Mishkan, means He is Shekhin here in the Aris.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.000
V'shakhanti v'tokham.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.000
That's what it says.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.000
It's extraordinary. The pasuq says,

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.000
V'asuli Mishkan.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:55.000
They should build for me a Mishkan, a tent.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.000
V'shakhanti.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.000
And my permanent address

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.000
would be with them.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.000
But do you take it literally, or maybe it's something else?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:09.000
I mean, as literal as it could be.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.000
This is the whole notion of the Mishkan.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.000
The whole notion of the V'tamikdash,

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.000
that the Jewish people have,

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.000
is to inverse

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Shamayim to Aris.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.000
The highest point of the universe,

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.000
therefore, is this earth.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.000
Why?

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.000
If you are, I don't know, in the middle of the universe,

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:35.000
where would you face up to?

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.000
To where God is, correct?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.000
Where God is.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.000
Here on the earth.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.000
This is the idea of the Mishkan.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Now you understand the idea of the Mishkan, right?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.000
And there's a simple theory behind it.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.000
Simple theory behind it.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.000
Rightly or wrongly.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
The simple theory is this.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:59.000
Out of all those celestial beings,

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.000
who may be intellectually superior to us,

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.000
may be more powerful, more intelligent, and so on,

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.000
there's a difference.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.000
Those beings are so great,

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.000
that they have no freedom of choice.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.000
They cannot choose.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.000
They are what they are.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.000
We, humans,

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.000
we are unique,

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.000
because we could choose.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
And therefore, in a sense,

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.000
