00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:34.000
Mishkan Ha'adut.

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:39.000
The Mishkan where the testimony is there.

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:41.000
And the other way,

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:42.000
it is called,

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:43.000
it is called

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:45.000
Ohel Moed.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.000
I'm going to explain each word,

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:48.000
and I'm going to explain

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:49.000
what each word represents,

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.000
and what does it mean exactly,

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:52.000
so you understand the temple,

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:53.000
how it operated.

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.000
We have Yamoshala Kohanim,

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.000
and one day I hope

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.000
that you or your children

00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:59.000
will be officiating

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:00.000
in the temple

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.000
that we're going to build.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:02.000
We're going to build it.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.000
Not this generation,

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.000
maybe next generation.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.000
We will build it.

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.000
And your children,

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:07.000
grandchildren,

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:08.000
you can never tell,

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:09.000
maybe his children,

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.000
little aunt,

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:12.000
you know,

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:13.000
you can never tell.

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:15.000
It's going to happen there.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:16.000
Alright, now,

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:17.000
very important.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:18.000
Mishkan,

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.000
Mishkan Adonai.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:23.000
Why is it called Mishkan Adonai?

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:25.000
Mishkan Adonai,

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:26.000
it represents,

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:27.000
I don't know if you remember,

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.000
in Mount Sinai,

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.000
there were three parts.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.000
The most important part

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:34.000
was the top of the Hasinai,

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
where God was there.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.000
And God was there,

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:39.000
and Moshe Rabbenu

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:40.000
was the only one

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.000
who was able

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.000
to ascend all the way

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:45.000
to the top of Mount Sinai,

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:48.000
and speak mouth to mouth,

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:51.000
means face to face.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:52.000
In other words,

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:54.000
horizontally with God.

00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:55.000
And therefore,

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:56.000
this is called Mishkan Adonai

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.000
because here God dwells.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:00.000
That is the top of the world,

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.000
in a sense.

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:04.000
And once a year,

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:08.000
the Kohen Gadol could come.

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:09.000
Moshe Rabbenu could come

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.000
any time he wants to.

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:13.000
But if not Moshe Rabbenu,

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:15.000
the Kohen Gadol,

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:16.000
once a year,

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.000
he could come and speak

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:21.000
with God who dwells there.

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:22.000
And no matter what questions,

00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:23.000
what problem,

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:24.000
what,

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:26.000
you have total access to God.

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:29.000
And via the Kohen Gadol,

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:31.000
the rest of the Jewish people

00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:33.000
knows everything they want to know.

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:34.000
There is nothing,

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:36.000
nothing which is

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:38.000
barred from the Jewish people

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:41.000
because we have access to...

00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:43.000
And that's why it's called Mishkan Adonai,

00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:45.000
the place where God dwells.

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:46.000
And this represents

00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:48.000
the highest hierarchy of Judaism,

00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:50.000
which are the Kohanim.

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:51.000
Alright?

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:52.000
The Kohanim.

00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:54.000
And in the Temple,

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:55.000
you're going to see there are

00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:56.000
three parts in the Temple.

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:58.000
You have the Haser,

00:25:58.000 --> 00:25:59.000
which is the court.

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:01.000
Then you have the Qodesh.

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.000
And then you have the Qodesh HaKodeshim.

00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:04.000
I'll explain everything.

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:06.000
Qodesh HaKodeshim is that part

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:07.000
of the Temple

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:10.000
in which only Moshe Rabbenu

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:12.000
or Kohen Gadol in Yom Kippurim

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:14.000
is permitted to be.

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:18.000
And there is where God dwells.

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:20.000
Alright?

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:21.000
So therefore that's why it's called

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:22.000
Mishkan Adonai,

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:26.000
the residence of God.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:27.000
Alright.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.000
Second,

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:30.000
there's another word

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.000
by which the Mishkan is designated.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:36.000
It's called Mishkan Ha'edut.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:39.000
The Mishkan where the Ha'edut is.

00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:41.000
What is the Ha'edut?

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:44.000
The Ha'edut are the tablets

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:47.000
written with the finger of God

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:49.000
in which they have the Ten Commandments.

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:51.000
These are in the Ark.

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:52.000
But in order to understand exactly

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:53.000
how it works,

00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:54.000
in order to understand,

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:55.000
you have the Ark.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:58.000
The Ark is made of gold.

00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:01.000
And the tablets are there in the Ark.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:02.000
I'm telling you everything

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:03.000
which is in the parashyoth of today.

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:05.000
You know, the parashyoth of

00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:08.000
Barak Helte Pekudeh.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:10.000
You put the tablets there.

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.000
And then they are covered,

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:14.000
not with a regular cover,

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:16.000
but with something which is called kaporet.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:20.000
Kaporet is like a piece of gold

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:24.000
from which there are two keruvim,

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
two little angels

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.000
with the wings spread.

00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:29.000
Alright?

00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:30.000
You see,

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.000
part of the same...

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:39.000
They are not, you know, put together.

00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:42.000
They are part of the same block of gold.

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:43.000
Yes?

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:45.000
From the same there is the cover.

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:46.000
And from the same cover

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:49.000
it comes out two keruvim,

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:52.000
two baby angels with baby faces

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:54.000
with a wing spread.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:57.000
Now,

00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:58.000
what does it represent?

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:04.000
This wing spread is the footstool of God.

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:05.000
Let me explain to you.

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:09.000
You have a throne.

00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:12.000
And under the throne

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:15.000
you have a little bit like a cushion.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:18.000
So to speak,

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:21.000
HaShamaim Kis'o

00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:23.000
That's the way Yishai Yareth says it.

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:26.000
The throne goes up to heaven.

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:29.000
Ha'ares Hadom Raglad

00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:31.000
And in the earth,

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:32.000
which is in the Beta miqdash,

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:34.000
is the footstool.

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:35.000
You see?

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:36.000
So therefore,

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:39.000
the Eidut is like the link

00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:43.000
between God,

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.000
the highest form expression of God,

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:48.000
and the tablets.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:49.000
Alright?

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:51.000
So it's called Mishkan Eidut

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
because there you have the tablets,

00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:57.000
the covenant made between God and Israel

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.000
in Mount Sinai.

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:00.000
It is the document.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.000
It is a document.

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:02.000
So to speak,

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:04.000
signed by God.

00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:05.000
And establishing.

00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:06.000
And that's the Tora.

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:07.000
The Eidut.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:08.000
Alright?

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.000
Now,

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:10.000
this represents,

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:12.000
I don't know if you remember,

00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:16.000
when we were in Sinai,

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:17.000
there was a group,

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:18.000
Aharon,

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:19.000
and Moshe,

00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Nadav,

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:21.000
Abihu,

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:22.000
they went all the way to the top.

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.000
Moshe Rabbenu made it,

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.000
was the only one who made it,

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:25.000
all the way to the top.

00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:28.000
Then to the middle of the mountain,

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:32.000
there were the Shibaim Zekanim.

00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:33.000
The elder statements.

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:35.000
Who were the elder statements?

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:40.000
They were the legal representative

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:43.000
of Israel.

00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:47.000
We were represented by 70 statements.

00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:48.000
In other words,

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:51.000
they are our legal representative.

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:53.000
They were the members of the Sanhedrin,

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:56.000
they were the people who interpreted the law,

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:59.000
and the people who executed the law.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:00.000
Alright?

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.000
That's why,

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:07.000
this Eidut represents the second stage.

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:08.000
And these are,

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:09.000
we also have,

00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:10.000
we have Kohanim,

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:12.000
then we have Lebiim.

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:15.000
The Lebiim who are the one who teach the Tora.

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:16.000
You understand what I'm saying?

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:19.000
So therefore you have the Mishkan.

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:20.000
It's called one Mishkan

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:22.000
because it is the place where God lives.

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.000
Mishkan Eidut,

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:25.000
because it's the tablets,

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:26.000
the testimony,

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
the covenant,

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:29.000
the document,

00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:31.000
written and signed by God,

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:33.000
and Israel, so to speak,

00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:35.000
that is the document.

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:37.000
And this represents the legal apparatus

00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:39.000
of the Jewish people.

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.000
When we were in Sinai,

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:41.000
there were the Zekanim

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.000
in the middle of the mountain.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.000
Alright?

00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:45.000
And then you have,

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:46.000
in the Metavigdash,

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:49.000
you have something which is called Qodesh.

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:50.000
You have Qodesh HaKorashim,

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:51.000
which is the highest,

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:52.000
then you have the Qodesh.

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:53.000
The Qodesh is the place

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:55.000
where is the altar,

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:57.000
and when you bring the Korbanot,

00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:59.000
service to God.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:01.000
And then there is,

00:31:01.000 --> 00:31:02.000
is another way

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.000
in which the Mishkan is called,

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:07.000
is called Ohel HaEidut.

00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:09.000
No longer Mishkan,

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:11.000
because Mishkan is the residence of God,

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.000
but Ohel, a tent,

00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:17.000
where the people assemble

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:20.000
to discuss

00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:23.000
whatever national crisis happens to be.

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.000
When there was a national crisis

00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:27.000
among the Jewish people,

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:29.000
the Jewish people met

00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:32.000
in Ohel HaEidut,

00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:35.000
in the tent,

00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:36.000
like in the Knesset,

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:37.000
like to the Knesset,

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:39.000
but that was made by the people.

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:40.000
That was the people,

00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:41.000
that was mostly like a,

00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:43.000
like an assembly hall in America,

00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:45.000
in which the whole town,

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.000
like a town meeting hall.

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.000
And therefore, the Ohel Mo'ed

00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:51.000
is the Ohel in which Mo'ed,

00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:52.000
in the sense,

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.000
B'twa'adu.

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:55.000
You see, you understand Arabic?

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:56.000
B'twa'adu, there,

00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:58.000
means where they convey,

00:31:58.000 --> 00:31:59.000
they meet.

00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:00.000
B'twa'adu, that's the word.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.000
Ohel Mo'ed, literally means

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:05.000
the place in which the Jewish people

00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:08.000
B'twa'adu, they congregate.

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:10.000
That would be the word in English.

00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:11.000
They congregate there.

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:14.000
And that represents

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:15.000
the rest of the people

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:19.000
at the foot of Mount Sinai.

00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:20.000
You see, there were three,

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:22.000
there were two people on the top,

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:23.000
people in the middle,

00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:25.000
people at the bottom.

00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:26.000
And this also,

00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:28.000
you have another equivalent like this

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:30.000
in the Mishkan,

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:32.000
which is the Haser,

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:34.000
the courtyard in the Mishkan,

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:36.000
in which every Jew,

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:38.000
man and woman,

00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:40.000
were permitted to enter.

00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:42.000
And the same thing you have

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:43.000
in the Bet ha-Miqdash,

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:45.000
you had the Qodesh HaKorashim,

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:47.000
you had the Qodesh,

00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:49.000
and then you have HaAzara.

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:52.000
HaAzara is where everybody,

00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:53.000
men and women,

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:56.000
are permitted to enter there.

00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:57.000
Alright?

00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:58.000
Yes, Maurice.

00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:00.000
Ohel, Ha'adu, and Ohel Mo'ed,

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.000
the same thing?

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Yes.

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:03.000
Ohel, the same thing,

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:06.000
is the place where the people congregate.

00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:07.000
But it's interesting,

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:10.000
there it's no longer called a Mishkan.

00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:11.000
You see?

00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:13.000
It's called an Ohel.

00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:16.000
Because Mishkan is vis-a-vis God.

00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.000
Although it's the same place,

00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:21.000
it's the same spot,

00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:22.000
you know,

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.000
but the name varies.

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:25.000
So they call it this.

00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:29.000
I want you to know this thing.

00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:30.000
Alright?

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.000
Now.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:32.000
Alright.

00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:38.000
Yes.

00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:42.000
No.

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:43.000
No.

00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:44.000
Later on,

00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:45.000
Sareeha.

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:46.000
No and yes.

